    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nNeovim's default nohl mapping is `C-l` instead of `C-L`.",
    "closed_at": "2023-03-23T15:01:06Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Does this PR fixes something for you which doesn't work right now?\r\n\r\nI think it is correct as is, mainly for two reasons:\r\n- Case of second key in ctrl mappings doesn't matter for creating keymap. Like `<C-l>` and `<C-L>` both represent same combination of keys.\r\n- Usage of `<C-L>` instead of `<C-l>` is prompted by the fact that this is how `vim.api.nvim_get_keymap()` returns this key combo.",
