        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Does this PR fixes something for you which doesn't work right now?\r\n> \r\n> I think it is correct as is, mainly for two reasons:\r\n> \r\n>     * Case of second key in ctrl mappings doesn't matter for creating keymap. Like `<C-l>` and `<C-L>` both represent same combination of keys.\r\n> \r\n>     * Usage of `<C-L>` instead of `<C-l>` is prompted by the fact that this is how `vim.api.nvim_get_keymap()` returns this key combo.\r\n\r\nMhm, for me without this change the `C-l` mapping didn't work when I wanted to hide the search highlights after a search. However, I see your point as well and it might be a side-effect of some weird combinations from my local setup now (kitty, neovim 0.8.3 or some other plugins) I'll try to come up with a minimal reproducible example later today.",
