            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "What does `:nmap <C-l>` show without this PR's change?\r\n\r\nIf you enabled `mappings.windows` then `<C-l>` is overwritten as `<C-w>l` for more coherent window navigation. So If you want to use window navigation mappings, you can not enable them in the `setup()` and instead put modified [version of the source code](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/basics.lua#L627) in your config.",
